          {
            "id": "p18-q11-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use the quadratic formula on ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "s^2-2s-2=0",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and take the positive root.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $s>0$ be the original side length, in units.\n$$\\begin{align*}(s+2)^2&=3s^2\\\\s^2+4s+4&=3s^2\\\\2s^2-4s-4&=0\\\\s^2-2s-2&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nWith $a=1$, $b=-2$ and $c=-2$, the quadratic formula gives\n$$\\begin{align*}s&=\\frac{-(-2)\\pm\\sqrt{(-2)^2-4(1)(-2)}}{2(1)}\\\\s&=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{12}}{2}\\\\s&=1\\pm\\sqrt3.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $1-\\sqrt3<0$, the original side length is $1+\\sqrt3$ units.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 86
